\title{healthexpectancies: Functions to calculate Health and Disability-free Life Expectancies (DFLE) using Sullivan method}
\description{
The package provides useful functions to calculate Disability-free Life Expectancies (DFLE) using Sullivan method. Calculations are based on Newcastle University's Practical Guide, initially created in the Euro-REVES project and subsequently updated with funding from the European Commission for the European Health Expectancy Monitoring Unit (EHEMU) and the European Health and Life Expectancy Information System (EHLEIS). The package also includes present and forecasted data tables for France, functions that smooth prevalences observed by age bracket, and functions that project prevalences and DFLE, under hypotheses on the evolution of DFLE or with models estimated on past observations.
